lerplate Outpost","Gearpost Outpost","Signal Hill Outpost","Coalseam Outpost","Tinlode Outpost","Silverseam Outpost"]},"desc":{"victorian":["where the mill hooters wake the whole town at five","whose canal runs blue on Mondays and red on Thursdays, depending on the dye works","built around a cotton mill the size of a cathedral","where every chimney has a name and a rival","famous for its brass band and its terrible weather","whose mayor made his fortune in buttons","where the foundry glow lights the streets all night","whose town hall clock is always seven minutes fast","built on seven hills and twelve coal seams","where the trams run on steam and good manners","whose market sells pies, pocket watches and second-hand boilers","where the soot falls like black snow every winter","famous for its engine works and its brass-domed library","whose workers' cottages climb the valley in neat grey rows","where the Great Hall shows off a new invention every spring","whose ironmasters meet in secret in the back room of the Mechanics' Hall","where the river has been bridged forty times and paved over twice","whose railway station is grander than most palaces","where the Saturday football crowds are louder than the steam hammers","built by a mill-owner who wanted a town in his own image","whose glassworks make the finest goggle lenses in the land","where the lamp-men go on strike every Michaelmas","whose smoke can be seen from three counties away","where children learn to read from patent-machine catalogues","famous for its mustard, its mills and its marvellous engines"],"airship":["where a hundred mooring masts rise above the rooftops","whose harbourmaster has never once set foot on the ground","where cargo balloons queue for hours above the chimneys","famous for its windsock market and its sky-sailors' chapel","whose gasworks fill a thousand envelopes a day","where the weather forecast is shouted from the top of the tallest mast","built around a mooring tower taller than any cathedral","whose docks hang from the clifftop on iron chains","where passengers board by basket, lift or very long ladder","whose customs men fly patrol kites over the harbour","where every inn has a balcony for parking airships","famous for its airship races and its fearless riggers","whose skyline is crowded with gondolas and gasbags","where the post office has its own fleet of dirigibles","whose clock tower doubles as a mooring mast at noon","where ropes, pulleys and winches hum day and night","built on a plateau where the winds always blow favourably","whose sail-lofts stitch envelopes from the finest silk","where captains swap tall tales over strong tea and crumpets","whose lighthouse shines upwards for ships in the clouds","where the cobbles are worn smooth by mooring cables","famous for its balloon-makers and its windy afternoons","whose guild of riggers is older than the city itself","where the gentry arrive by private airship every summer","that holds a grand air fair every midsummer"],"clockwork":["where the streets rearrange themselves every hour on the hour","built inside the workings of an enormous clock","whose bridges rise and fall to the tick of a great pendulum","where every citizen carries a key to wind the city up","whose towers turn slowly to follow the sun","where the trams run on springs and never quite stop","whose great clock has not lost a second in two hundred years","where the guild of watchmakers rules from a glass tower","built on a giant turntable that makes one turn a day","whose fountains are powered by falling weights","where the bells play a different tune every quarter hour","whose automaton guards wear bowler hats and polished brass","where the moon is tracked by an orrery the size of a cathedral","that must be wound by hand once a year at midsummer","where every doorway clicks open with a tiny brass key","whose market stalls fold away into the walls at dusk","where the whole city stops for one silent minute at noon","whose gears can be heard humming beneath the pavements","built by a clockmaker who wanted to measure eternity","where time runs slightly faster on the east side","whose streetlamps light one after another like the hand of a clock","where the cogwheel mill grinds flour, pepper and time","whose clockwork birds sing the hours from every rooftop","where children set their watches by the great bell, Old Tom","famous for its musical clocks and its mechanical gardens"],"smog":["where the fog is so thick that the lamps burn all day","built in the old sewers beneath a grander city","whose people have not seen a clear sky in three generations","where gas lamps light tunnels that go on for miles","whose market is held in a flooded railway cutting","where the smog is sold in jars to curious tourists","reached by a steam lift that creaks all the way down","whose rooftops are the cellars of the city above","where the chimney sweeps run the town council","whose canals run through tunnels lit by glow-lanterns","where everyone wears goggles and a scarf all year round","built in a flooded coal mine pumped dry by great engines","whose fog horns sound every hour to warn the boats","where the pipes hiss, clank and groan all night","whose lamp-makers are the richest folk in town","where the trains run beneath the streets in clouds of steam","built in the brick arches under an old railway viaduct","whose sky is the underside of a great iron bridge","where the only sunlight arrives through a single grating","whose mushroom farms feed the whole city above","where the smoke from a thousand chimneys gathers in the hollow","whose tunnels are marked with chalk arrows and hope","where the rain comes down black and the cats come out grey","whose underground river carries coal barges to the sea","known for its fogbound alleys and friendly lamplit pubs"],"frontier":["a railhead town at the very end of the line","built around a telegraph post on the edge of the map","where prospectors trade brass and copper for supplies","whose fort has steam-cannon on every corner","founded by an explorer who refused to go any further","where the stagecoaches have been replaced by steam-wagons","famous for its geysers, which power the whole town","whose governor rules from a walking iron mansion","where airships drop mail and news once a fortnight","built on a copper seam that runs for a hundred miles","whose engineers are laying a railway across the desert","where the general store sells everything from tea to telescopes","whose water tower is the tallest thing for fifty miles","where the dust storms are as thick as the fog back home","founded by a society of gentlemen geologists","whose clockwork mules carry ore down from the hills","where the brass band plays the governor's favourite march every evening","built at the meeting of three rivers and two railways","whose saloon serves tea with a dash of steam","where a steam-powered paddle boat brings supplies upriver","whose surveyors have mapped everything but the way home","where the frontier ends and the unexplored begins","whose windmills pump water from deep beneath the plains","on the edge of an unexplored jungle full of strange machines","where a dozen company flags fly over one dusty high street"]}}}